IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fca-nouns`
IMPORT `fca-definitions`
IMPORT `fca-s3-application`
IMPORT `fca-s2-adjustment`
IMPORT `fca-seat`

-- Frustrated Contracts Act 1959 (Singapore) -- WORKED CASES for the seat layer: one or more per question, in the seat's order.
-- The seat is a party to a contract that has become impossible to perform.  Every case is the facts such a person would state,
-- and its expected answer is written beside it, from the text of the Act, before the run.  A failing assertion is a finding.
-- The base facts of every case, unless the case says otherwise: a contract frustrated and discharged on 1 June 2020, made on 1 January 2000,
-- not a charterparty, not insurance, not a sale of goods, the Government not a party; a sum of 1000 paid (or payable) in pursuance of the contract
-- before the discharge; expenses of 300 incurred by the receiving party; the court considers it just to let them keep 200; a valuable benefit
-- worth 5000 with 100 retained under s 2(3); a sum of 4000 the court considers just for the benefit; insurance money payable because of
-- the frustration with no obligation to insure; a contract provision for the event of frustration; section 2 would give 100 of which the
-- court finds 60 consistent; a wholly performed part the court finds can properly be severed.


§ `Does section 2 operate on my contract? (s 2(1))`
-- Does section 2 have effect on my contract [the base facts]: the contract is frustrated and the parties were discharged on 1 June 2020, and no exclusion in s 3 applies.
#ASSERT `Does section 2 have effect on my contract` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Does section 2 have effect on my contract [frustrated = FALSE]: "Where a contract has become impossible of performance or been otherwise frustrated": not met.
#ASSERT `Does section 2 have effect on my contract` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Does section 2 have effect on my contract [discharged = FALSE]: "and the parties ... have for that reason been discharged": not met.
#ASSERT `Does section 2 have effect on my contract` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Does section 2 have effect on my contract [charter = TRUE]: a voyage charterparty: s 3(5)(a) "This Act shall not apply".
#ASSERT `Does section 2 have effect on my contract` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Does section 2 have effect on my contract [dis_date = (Date 31 12 1958)]: discharged before 1 January 1959: s 3(1) "but not to contracts as respects which the time of discharge is before that date".
#ASSERT `Does section 2 have effect on my contract` TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 1958) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Money paid, or payable, under the contract (s 2(2) and (3))`
-- Can I get back money I paid [the base facts]: money paid under the contract before the discharge is recoverable from the recipient.
#ASSERT `Can I get back money I paid` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Can I get back money I paid [sum_before = FALSE]: paid after the discharge: "before the time when the parties were so discharged" is a time the text fixes in its own words, so a sum outside it is JUST FALSE (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Can I get back money I paid` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Can I get back money I paid [sum_pursuance = FALSE]: not paid in pursuance of the contract: outside the subsection.
#ASSERT `Can I get back money I paid` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Can I get back money I paid [insurance = TRUE]: a contract of insurance: s 3(5)(b), so section 2 has no effect.
#ASSERT `Can I get back money I paid` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Do sums I had to pay stop being payable [the base facts]: a sum payable before the discharge ceases to be payable.
#ASSERT `Do sums I had to pay stop being payable` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Do sums I had to pay stop being payable [sum_before = FALSE]: fell payable after the discharge: outside the time bound, JUST FALSE (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Do sums I had to pay stop being payable` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Can the court allow the other party to keep or recover [the base facts]: expenses were incurred and the court considers it just.
#ASSERT `Can the court allow the other party to keep or recover` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Can the court allow the other party to keep or recover [exp_incurred = FALSE]: "If the party ... incurred expenses": not met.
#ASSERT `Can the court allow the other party to keep or recover` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Can the court allow the other party to keep or recover [court_just3 = No]: "if it considers it just": the court does not.
#ASSERT `Can the court allow the other party to keep or recover` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Can the court allow the other party to keep or recover [court_just3 = `I am not sure`]: the court has not yet said whether it considers it just.
#ASSERT `Can the court allow the other party to keep or recover` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- What is the most the court may allow [the base facts]: expenses of 300, sum of 1000: not more than the expenses.
#ASSERT `What is the most the court may allow` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 0 0 EQUALS JUST 300
-- What is the most the court may allow [exp_overhead = 50, exp_personal = 25]: expenses 300 plus 50 overhead plus 25 personal work, as estimated under s 2(5).
#ASSERT `What is the most the court may allow` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 50 25 EQUALS JUST 375
-- What is the most the court may allow [exp_amount = 2000]: expenses of 2000 exceed the sum: the whole of the sums is the most.
#ASSERT `What is the most the court may allow` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE 2000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- What is the most the court may allow [exp_incurred = FALSE]: no expenses incurred: no power, so no ceiling.
#ASSERT `What is the most the court may allow` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 300 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Is the amount the court allowed within the limit [allowed = 300]: 300 equals the expenses of 300.
#ASSERT `Is the amount the court allowed within the limit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 0 0 300 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Is the amount the court allowed within the limit [allowed = 301]: "not being an amount in excess of the expenses so incurred".
#ASSERT `Is the amount the court allowed within the limit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 0 0 301 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together [paid 2000, still to pay 3000, expenses 4000]: 2,000 paid and 3,000 still to pay, 5,000 in all, against expenses of 4,000: one ceiling for the sums together, so 4,000 and not 2,000 + 3,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2000 3000 TRUE TRUE 4000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 4000
-- What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together [paid 1000, still to pay 500, expenses 4000]: a total below the expenses: the total is the most.
#ASSERT `What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 500 TRUE TRUE 4000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 1500
-- What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together [paid 2000, still to pay 3000, expenses 1000]: a total above the expenses: the expenses are the most.
#ASSERT `What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2000 3000 TRUE TRUE 1000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together [paid 0, still to pay 3000, expenses 4000]: nothing paid, 3,000 still to pay: the one sum is the total.
#ASSERT `What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 3000 TRUE TRUE 4000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 3000
-- What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together [every sum counted = FALSE]: the sums counted were not all paid or payable in pursuance of the contract before the discharge: none is a sum s 2(2) reaches, so there is no total.
#ASSERT `What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2000 3000 FALSE TRUE 4000 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together [no expenses]: no expenses incurred: the power does not arise.
#ASSERT `What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2000 3000 TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together [insurance = TRUE]: a contract of insurance: section 2 has no effect.
#ASSERT `What is the most the court may allow from all the sums together` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2000 3000 TRUE TRUE 4000 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Is the amount the court allowed from all the sums together within the limit [allowed 4000]: 4,000 allowed out of 5,000 in all against expenses of 4,000: within the limit.
#ASSERT `Is the amount the court allowed from all the sums together within the limit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2000 3000 TRUE TRUE 4000 0 0 4000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Is the amount the court allowed from all the sums together within the limit [allowed 4001]: 4,001 allowed: "in excess of the expenses so incurred".
#ASSERT `Is the amount the court allowed from all the sums together within the limit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2000 3000 TRUE TRUE 4000 0 0 4001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Is the amount the court allowed from all the sums together within the limit [allowed 5000]: 5,000 allowed (2,000 + 3,000 added) exceeds the expenses of 4,000: not within the limit.
#ASSERT `Is the amount the court allowed from all the sums together within the limit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2000 3000 TRUE TRUE 4000 0 0 5000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Is the amount the court allowed from all the sums together within the limit [expenses 6000, allowed 5001]: 5,001 allowed out of 5,000 in all, within the expenses of 6,000: above the sums, so not any part of them.
#ASSERT `Is the amount the court allowed from all the sums together within the limit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2000 3000 TRUE TRUE 6000 0 0 5001 EQUALS NOTHING
-- How much of the money I paid can I get back [the base facts]: paid 1000, the court allows 200 to be kept: 800 is recoverable.
#ASSERT `How much of the money I paid can I get back` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 0 0 Yes TRUE 200 EQUALS JUST 800
-- How much of the money I paid can I get back [decided = FALSE]: the court has not said how much it allows.
#ASSERT `How much of the money I paid can I get back` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 0 0 Yes FALSE 200 EQUALS NOTHING
-- How much of the money I paid can I get back [court_just3 = No]: the court does not consider it just to allow anything: the whole sum is recoverable.
#ASSERT `How much of the money I paid can I get back` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 0 0 No TRUE 200 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- How much of the money I paid can I get back [allowed = 301]: an allowance above the expenses is not one the Act provides for.
#ASSERT `How much of the money I paid can I get back` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 0 0 Yes TRUE 301 EQUALS NOTHING
-- How much of a sum I was to pay remains payable [the base facts]: a sum of 1000 ceased to be payable; the court allows 200 to be recovered: 200 remains payable.
#ASSERT `How much of a sum I was to pay remains payable` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 0 0 Yes TRUE 200 EQUALS JUST 200
-- How much of a sum I was to pay remains payable [court_just3 = No]: the court allows nothing: nothing remains payable.
#ASSERT `How much of a sum I was to pay remains payable` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 0 0 No TRUE 200 EQUALS JUST 0

§ `A valuable benefit (s 2(4))`
-- Can a sum be recovered for a valuable benefit [the base facts]: a valuable benefit obtained before the discharge by reason of what the other party did.
#ASSERT `Can a sum be recovered for a valuable benefit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Can a sum be recovered for a valuable benefit [ben_before = FALSE]: obtained after the discharge: the "where" is not met.
#ASSERT `Can a sum be recovered for a valuable benefit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Can a sum be recovered for a valuable benefit [ben_obtained = FALSE]: no benefit obtained: the "where" is not met.
#ASSERT `Can a sum be recovered for a valuable benefit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Can a sum be recovered for a valuable benefit [ben_money = TRUE]: "(other than a payment of money to which subsection (2) applies)" is part of what the "Where" describes: a payment to which s 2(2) applies is a "where" not met, JUST FALSE (judgment call QE).
#ASSERT `Can a sum be recovered for a valuable benefit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- What is the most that can be recovered for the benefit [the base facts]: not exceeding the value of the benefit to the party obtaining it.
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be recovered for the benefit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 5000 EQUALS JUST 5000
-- Is the sum the court considers just within the limit [sum_just = 5000]: 5000 does not exceed the value of 5000.
#ASSERT `Is the sum the court considers just within the limit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 5000 5000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Is the sum the court considers just within the limit [sum_just = 5001]: "not exceeding the value of that benefit".
#ASSERT `Is the sum the court considers just within the limit` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 5000 5001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- What expenses must the court have regard to [the base facts]: expenses 300 plus 100 retained or recoverable under s 2(3).
#ASSERT `What expenses must the court have regard to` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 TRUE 300 0 0 EQUALS JUST 400
-- Must the court have regard to this matter [the base facts]: paragraph (a): the expenses are a matter the court has regard to.
#ASSERT `Must the court have regard to this matter` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `The expenses the party who obtained the benefit incurred` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Must the court have regard to this matter [matter = `Something that is not a circumstance of the case`]: "all the circumstances of the case": what is not one is outside the instruction.
#ASSERT `Must the court have regard to this matter` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `Something that is not a circumstance of the case` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Expenses (s 2(5))`
-- What are the expenses as the court estimates them [the base facts]: expenses of 300 and nothing included for overheads or personal work.
#ASSERT `What are the expenses as the court estimates them` TRUE 300 0 0 EQUALS JUST 300
-- What are the expenses as the court estimates them [exp_overhead = 50, exp_personal = 25]: 300 plus 50 plus 25.
#ASSERT `What are the expenses as the court estimates them` TRUE 300 50 25 EQUALS JUST 375
-- What are the expenses as the court estimates them [exp_incurred = FALSE]: no expenses incurred: nothing to estimate.
#ASSERT `What are the expenses as the court estimates them` FALSE 300 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- May the court include overheads and my own work [the base facts]: the court may include a reasonable sum for overheads and personal work.
#ASSERT `May the court include overheads and my own work` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- May the court include overheads and my own work [frustrated = FALSE]: section 2 has no effect on a contract that is not frustrated.
#ASSERT `May the court include overheads and my own work` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Insurance money (s 2(6))`
-- Must the court leave insurance money out of account [the base facts]: insurance money became payable because of the frustration and there was no obligation to insure: the court shall not take it into account.
#ASSERT `Must the court leave insurance money out of account` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Must the court leave insurance money out of account [ins_express = TRUE]: "unless there was an obligation to insure imposed by an express term": the bar does not apply.
#ASSERT `Must the court leave insurance money out of account` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Must the court leave insurance money out of account [ins_enactment = TRUE]: "or by or under any enactment": the bar does not apply.
#ASSERT `Must the court leave insurance money out of account` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Must the court leave insurance money out of account [ins_sums = FALSE]: no insurance money of the kind described: outside the bar.
#ASSERT `Must the court leave insurance money out of account` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- May the court take insurance money into account [the base facts]: the bar applies: "the court shall not take into account".
#ASSERT `May the court take insurance money into account` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- May the court take insurance money into account [ins_express = TRUE]: the exception lifts the bar but the Act does not itself say the court may count the money.
#ASSERT `May the court take insurance money into account` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `A benefit given to someone else (s 2(7))`
-- May the court treat the benefit as obtained by the person who took on the obligations [the base facts]: a person assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on someone else; the court considers it just.
#ASSERT `May the court treat the benefit as obtained by the person who took on the obligations` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- May the court treat the benefit as obtained by the person who took on the obligations [ob_party = TRUE]: "whether a party to the contract or not": the same answer.
#ASSERT `May the court treat the benefit as obtained by the person who took on the obligations` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- May the court treat the benefit as obtained by the person who took on the obligations [court_just7 = No]: "if ... it considers it just": the court does not.
#ASSERT `May the court treat the benefit as obtained by the person who took on the obligations` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- May the court treat the benefit as obtained by the person who took on the obligations [ob_assumed = FALSE]: "Where any person has assumed obligations under the contract": not met.
#ASSERT `May the court treat the benefit as obtained by the person who took on the obligations` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- May the court treat the benefit as obtained by the person who took on the obligations [court_just7 = `I am not sure`]: the court has not yet said.
#ASSERT `May the court treat the benefit as obtained by the person who took on the obligations` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Does the Act apply to my contract? (s 3(1) and (2), and s 3 as a whole)`
-- Does the Act apply to my contract [the base facts]: discharged in 2020; no exclusion applies.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my contract` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Does the Act apply to my contract [dis_date = (Date 31 12 1958)]: s 3(1): discharged before 1 January 1959.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my contract` TRUE (Date 31 12 1958) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Does the Act apply to my contract [dis_date = (Date 1 1 1959)]: s 3(1): discharged on 1 January 1959, "on or after".
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my contract` TRUE (Date 1 1 1959) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Does the Act apply to my contract [insurance = TRUE]: s 3(5)(b).
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my contract` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Does the Act apply to my contract [charter = TRUE, time = TRUE]: a time charterparty is excepted from s 3(5)(a), and no other exclusion applies.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my contract` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Does the Act apply to my contract [specific = TRUE, perished = FALSE]: a sale of specific goods not frustrated by their perishing: s 3(5)(c) does not catch it.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my contract` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Does the Act apply to my contract [discharged = FALSE]: the parties have not been discharged: there is no time of discharge to apply s 3(1) to.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my contract` FALSE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Does the Act reach my contract by its discharge date [the base facts]: discharged 1 June 2020.
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my contract by its discharge date` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Does the Act reach my contract by its discharge date [dis_date = (Date 31 12 1958)]: the day before 1 January 1959.
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my contract by its discharge date` TRUE (Date 31 12 1958) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Does the Act reach my contract by its discharge date [dis_date = (Date 1 1 1959)]: "on or after 1 January 1959".
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my contract by its discharge date` TRUE (Date 1 1 1959) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Does it matter when my contract was made [made_date = (Date 12 2 1959)]: "whether made before or after 13 February 1959": before.
#ASSERT `Does it matter when my contract was made` (Date 12 2 1959) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Does it matter when my contract was made [made_date = (Date 14 2 1959)]: "whether made before or after 13 February 1959": after.
#ASSERT `Does it matter when my contract was made` (Date 14 2 1959) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Does the Act apply to my Government contract in the same way [gov = TRUE]: the Government is a party: the Act applies in like manner.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my Government contract in the same way` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Does the Act apply to my Government contract in the same way [the base facts]: no Government party: outside the subsection.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my Government contract in the same way` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `My contract's own terms, and a part already performed (s 3(3) and (4))`
-- Must the court give effect to my contract's own provision [the base facts]: the contract has a provision for the event of frustration: the court shall give effect to it.
#ASSERT `Must the court give effect to my contract's own provision` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Must the court give effect to my contract's own provision [prov_event = FALSE, prov_always = FALSE]: "Where any contract ... contains any provision": not met.
#ASSERT `Must the court give effect to my contract's own provision` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Must the court give effect to my contract's own provision [prov_event = FALSE, prov_always = TRUE]: "or is intended to have effect whether such circumstances arise or not".
#ASSERT `Must the court give effect to my contract's own provision` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Must the court give effect to my contract's own provision [insurance = TRUE]: "any contract to which this Act applies": an insurance contract is not one.
#ASSERT `Must the court give effect to my contract's own provision` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- How much of section 2 is given effect [the base facts]: section 2 would give 100; the court finds 60 consistent with the provision.
#ASSERT `How much of section 2 is given effect` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 100 TRUE 60 EQUALS JUST 60
-- How much of section 2 is given effect [cons_amount = 150]: never more than section 2 would otherwise give.
#ASSERT `How much of section 2 is given effect` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 100 TRUE 150 EQUALS JUST 100
-- How much of section 2 is given effect [cons_amount = 0]: "to such extent, if any": none.
#ASSERT `How much of section 2 is given effect` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 100 TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- How much of section 2 is given effect [cons_decided = FALSE]: the court has not said what is consistent.
#ASSERT `How much of section 2 is given effect` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 100 FALSE 60 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Must the court treat a performed part as a separate contract [the base facts]: a wholly performed part that the court finds can properly be severed.
#ASSERT `Must the court treat a performed part as a separate contract` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Yes TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Must the court treat a performed part as a separate contract [sev_view = No]: "Where it appears to the court that a part ... can properly be severed": it does not.
#ASSERT `Must the court treat a performed part as a separate contract` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE No TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Must the court treat a performed part as a separate contract [sev_view = `I am not sure`]: the court has not said.
#ASSERT `Must the court treat a performed part as a separate contract` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Must the court treat a performed part as a separate contract [sev_wholly = FALSE, sev_butpay = TRUE]: "or so performed except for the payment ... of sums which are or can be ascertained".
#ASSERT `Must the court treat a performed part as a separate contract` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Yes FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Must the court treat a performed part as a separate contract [sev_wholly = FALSE, sev_butpay = FALSE]: the part was not performed in either way.
#ASSERT `Must the court treat a performed part as a separate contract` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Yes FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Does section 2 apply to this portion of my contract [the base facts]: "section 2 as only applicable to the remainder": not to the severed part.
#ASSERT `Does section 2 apply to this portion of my contract` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Yes TRUE FALSE `The part treated as a separate contract` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Does section 2 apply to this portion of my contract [portion = `The rest of my contract`]: section 2 applies to the remainder.
#ASSERT `Does section 2 apply to this portion of my contract` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Yes TRUE FALSE `The rest of my contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Does section 2 apply to this portion of my contract [sev_view = No]: the severance rule does not apply: s 3(4) says nothing about either portion.
#ASSERT `Does section 2 apply to this portion of my contract` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE No TRUE FALSE `The part treated as a separate contract` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Am I outside the Act? (s 3(5))`
-- Am I outside the Act as a charterparty or sea carriage [charter = TRUE]: a charterparty that is neither a time charterparty nor by way of demise.
#ASSERT `Am I outside the Act as a charterparty or sea carriage` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Am I outside the Act as a charterparty or sea carriage [charter = TRUE, time = TRUE]: "except a time charterparty": excepted from the paragraph.
#ASSERT `Am I outside the Act as a charterparty or sea carriage` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Am I outside the Act as a charterparty or sea carriage [charter = TRUE, demise = TRUE]: "or a charterparty by way of demise": excepted from the paragraph.
#ASSERT `Am I outside the Act as a charterparty or sea carriage` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Am I outside the Act as a charterparty or sea carriage [carriage = TRUE]: a contract, other than a charterparty, for the carriage of goods by sea.
#ASSERT `Am I outside the Act as a charterparty or sea carriage` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Am I outside the Act as a charterparty or sea carriage [the base facts]: neither a charterparty nor a contract for the carriage of goods by sea.
#ASSERT `Am I outside the Act as a charterparty or sea carriage` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Am I outside the Act as an insurance contract [insurance = TRUE]: a contract of insurance.
#ASSERT `Am I outside the Act as an insurance contract` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Am I outside the Act as an insurance contract [the base facts]: not a contract of insurance.
#ASSERT `Am I outside the Act as an insurance contract` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Does section 2(6) still apply to my insurance contract [insurance = TRUE]: "except as is provided by section 2(6)": section 2(6) still applies.
#ASSERT `Does section 2(6) still apply to my insurance contract` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Does section 2(6) still apply to my insurance contract [the base facts]: not a contract of insurance: the exception is not engaged.
#ASSERT `Does section 2(6) still apply to my insurance contract` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
